1
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
When the young gets tough, the tough gets going!

2
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Young Rebels is a action film directed by Amir Shervan.

3
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
From Amir Shervan, the director of SAMURAI COP, comes
another great 90's action classic.

4
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
One man (Johnny Greene) teams up with another (Tadashi Yamashita) to take
down the cartel run and its evil leader (Robert Z'Dar).

5
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Charlie, played by Jon Greene.

6
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Genza, played by Tadashi Yamashita.

7
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Joey Vincenzo, played by Robert Z'Dar.

8
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Sheriff, played by Aldo Ray.

9
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Liz, played by Christine Lunde.

10
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Deputy Judd, played by Dale Cummings.

11
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
The Killer (Chinese: 喋血雙雄) is a 1989 Hong Kong action film
directed by John Woo, and produced by Tsui Hark.

12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
The film stars Chow Yun-fat, Danny Lee, and Sally Yeh.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Chow plays Ah Jong, a professional assassin for the Triads who wants to retire, but accidentally damages the eyes of
singer Jennie (Yeh) during a shootout and sets out to perform one last hit to pay for her treatment.

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
After the financial backing from Hark became problematic following the release of Woo's film A Better
Tomorrow 2, Woo had to find backing through Chow Yun-fat's and Danny Lee's financing companies.

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Woo went into filming The Killer with a rough draft whose plot was
influenced by the films Le Samouraï, Mean Streets and Narazumono.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
Woo wanted to make a film about honour, friendship and the
relationship of two seemingly opposite people.

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
After finishing filming, Woo referred to The Killer as a tribute to
directors Jean-Pierre Melville and Martin Scorsese.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The Killer was not an immediate success in Hong Kong but received critical acclaim
internationally with reviewers praising its action scenes and over-the-top style.

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The film became Woo's steppingstone into Hollywood and has been a strong influence on many
directors, including Quentin Tarantino, Robert Rodriguez and Johnnie To.

20
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
In the years since, The Killer has come to be considered
one of the greatest action films ever made.

21
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
An English-language remake of the film, also directed
by Woo, was released in August 2024.
